{
  // Curated extract scene cues the game definitions do not describe - not served by the
  // tarkov.dev API. Hand-edited; `npm run eft:extracts` never writes this file.
  //
  // The location definitions behind extractRequirements.json5 carry each exit's mechanical
  // requirement, but not the in-world cues a player acts on: which sniper extracts need a
  // green signal flare, which exits show green smoke when open, and which doors need a key.
  // Each entry is keyed by tarkov.dev map ID, then tarkov.dev extract ID, and names the raw
  // exit name it was checked against. A cue never implies the exit is open in a given raid.
  //
  // Cue types: green_flare (fire a green flare first), flare (a flare whose color is not
  // confirmed), green_smoke (an availability signal, not an item to bring), key (with item).

  // Factory: Was: missing key cues. Current extraction table lists both locked doors.
  '55f2d3fd4bdc2d5f408b4567': {
